  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Factoring each choice completely makes its largest prime factor easy to identify:\n\\[\\begin{aligned}39&=3\\cdot13,\\\\51&=3\\cdot17,\\\\77&=7\\cdot11,\\\\91&=7\\cdot13,\\\\121&=11\\cdot11.\\end{aligned}\\]\nAll factors displayed are prime. Therefore the largest prime factors of choices A through E are \\(13,17,11,13,11\\), respectively. The greatest is \\(17\\), which belongs to \\(51\\), choice \\(\\mathrm B\\).",
